har</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Lam</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Potter</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ellis</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Sibbald</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Decreased capillary density <italic>in vivo </italic>in bowel mucosa of rats with normotensive sepsis</article-title><source>J Surg Res</source><year>1996</year><volume>61</volume><fpage>190</fpage><lpage>196</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8769965</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/jsre.1996.0103</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hersch</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Madorin</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Sibbald</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Selective gut microcirculatory control (SGMC) in septic rats: a novel approach with a locally applied vasoactive drug</article-title><source>Shock</source><year>1998</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>292</fpage><lpage>297</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9788662</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00024382-199810000-00010</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schinke</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Doods</surname><given-names>GD</given-names></name><name><surname>Wienen</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Entzeroth</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Characterization of rat intestinal angiotensin II receptors</article-title><source>Eur J Pharmacol</source><year>1991</year><volume>